{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"soppy-logophilic-husky","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The 20 s per-test hang budget kills xdist workers on every CI run\n\n## Symptom (pristine `origin/main` @ 6a5c88027c5, no other change applied)\n\nDefault suite, `pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.13)` — the ONLY leg that adds `--cov=rebar`:\n\n    run 32583448507 / job 97056277838: 11 failed, 16175 passed, 66 skipped in 1077.36s\n    run 32585303586 / job 97060825782: 11 failed, 16182 passed, 66 skipped in 1057.20s\n\nEvery failure is a worker death, each preceded by `[gwN] node down: Not properly terminated`:\n\n    worker 'gw2' crashed while running 'tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py::test_dropping_a_used_helpers_row_fails_loudly_instead_of_shrinking'\n    worker 'gw3' crashed while running 'tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py::test_safe_boundary_is_not_unwrapped_in_repository_tests'\n    worker 'gw1' crashed while running 'tests/scripts/test_binding_lifecycle_grace_seam_clean_heldout.py::test_gate_reports_no_findings_whole_tree'\n    ... 8 more, all whole-tree scanning gates ...\n\n`grep -c \"Failed: Timeout\"` = **0** in both jobs. Worker ids run gw0-gw12 under `-n 4`:\nxdist replaced each dead worker 11 times. The crashing SET is not stable between runs\n(`test_reconciler_jira_seam_clean_heldout` in one, `test_residual_drain_seam_clean_heldout`\nin the other), which is why it reads as flakiness.\n\nThe integration tier shows the same worker deaths (`node down: Not properly terminated` on\n3 of 4 nodes).\n\n## Root cause — CONFIRMED, reproduced deterministically\n\nCommit `6a5c88027c5` (story `bold-abeyant-indri` / 73b8-2d79-3046-44ce) lowered the per-test\nhang budget from **300 s to 20 s** in three places: `pyproject.toml:650` (`timeout = 20`, new\n`[tool.pytest.ini_options]` keys) and `_build-and-test.yml:662` + `:677`. `git blame -w -C -M`\non all three lines returns `6a5c88027c59` and nothing else.\n\n**Two facts combine.**\n\n1. **~14 legitimate tests genuinely cost more than 20 s on the runner.** The direct PARENT\n   commit `4d6c1cc835e`, same day, same runner class, same `-n 4 --dist worksteal --cov=rebar`,\n   under the OLD `--timeout=300` (run 32581500417 / job 97051623657, `16182 passed` in 906.38s,\n   zero crashes) reports in its own `--durations=25` block:\n\n       29.93s call  test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py::test_safe_boundary_is_not_unwrapped_in_repository_tests\n       28.72s call  test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py::test_dropping_a_used_helpers_row_fails_loudly_instead_of_shrinking\n       22.97s call  test_binding_lifecycle_grace_seam_clean_heldout.py::test_gate_reports_no_findings_whole_tree\n       22.63s call  test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py::test_main_on_real_tree_returns_zero\n       22.46s call  test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py::test_gate_reports_no_findings_for_owned_files\n       22.44s call  test_cli_seam_clean_heldout.py::test_gate_reports_no_findings_for_owned_files\n       21.63s call  test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py::test_real_source_tree_is_clean\n       ... 20.87s, 21.24s, 21.29s, 21.42s, 18.71s, 18.76s ...\n\n   That is the crash list. The data refuting \"20 s is measured\" was in CI at the parent commit.\n   These are `call` times, so `timeout_func_only = true` does not help: the body IS the scan.\n\n2. **`timeout_method = \"thread\"` expresses an expiry as `os._exit(1)`, not as a verdict.**\n   `pytest_timeout.py:542` (`timeout_timer`) calls `os._exit(1)` from the watchdog thread,\n   killing the xdist worker process outright. Only the `signal` method reports\n   `Failed: Timeout`, via `pytest.fail()` at `pytest_timeout.py:502`. So a budget expiry inside\n   a worker can NEVER surface as `Failed: Timeout` — it surfaces as `node down` + `worker\n   crashed`. The zero `Failed: Timeout` count is a PREDICTION of this mechanism, not evidence\n   against it. Bug `albinic-agrologic-dolphin` (0078-fa3e-05d1-4e12) proved this same mechanism\n   and used `--timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread` as its deliberate crash-INDUCING amplifier.\n\n**Positive feedback loop:** 11 worker restarts re-pay process + coverage startup, so the suite\nruns 1057-1077 s instead of 906 s and the SURVIVING scanners move from ~16 s to 19.0-19.95 s —\nright against the wall. Each crash makes the next more likely.\n\n**Local runtime proof** (worktree off 6a5c88027c5, macOS py3.12, three discriminating arms on a\n25 s-body probe test under `-n 2 --dist worksteal`):\n\n    ARM A  repo ini (timeout=20, thread)   -> [gw0] node down: Not properly terminated\n                                              worker 'gw0' crashed while running '<probe>'\n                                              zero `Failed: Timeout`      == the CI signature\n    ARM B  same budget, --timeout-method=signal -> `Failed: Timeout (>20.0s) from pytest-timeout.`\n                                              a clean verdict, worker survives\n    ARM C  pre-73b8 --timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread -> 2 passed in 25.88s\n\nArm B isolates the METHOD as what converts a timeout into a crash; Arm C isolates the BUDGET as\nwhat makes it fire at all. Coverage measured locally as a ~2x multiplier on these tests\n(2.91s -> 6.02s), which with the runner's slower cores is the rest of the gap.\n\n## Not attributable to any change in flight\n\nBoth failing runs are at headSha `6a5c88027c59d3e24d3e4269838fb3c591a64240` = pristine\n`origin/main`. Gerrit change 2098 (story 3436, compact-planner consolidation) touches only\n`src/rebar/_commands/compact_*.py` + two compact tests — none of the 11 crashing tests, and\nneither config file. It is NOT implicated; main itself is broken for every change.\n\n## Plan\n\nRestore the budget to the value bug `balsamy-eloquent-iggypops` (89d5-61da-b621-47f8)\nestablished and sized (\"300s dwarfs the slowest legitimate test\"), keeping story 73b8's\ngenuine improvement — the ini keys, so `make test` and a bare local `pytest` carry the budget\nCI does.\n\n1. `pyproject.toml` — `timeout = 20` -> `timeout = 300`, and update the sizing comment to cite\n   the measured 29.93 s worst case rather than the falsified \"runs clean at 20 s\" claim.\n2. `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:662` and `:677` — `--timeout=20` -> `--timeout=300`.\n   `test_the_shared_tier_lanes_carry_the_ini_timeout_budget` derives from the ini, so it\n   follows automatically.\n3. `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py` — `_INI_BUDGET_SECS` 20 -> 300, and RESTRUCTURE the\n   marker-override arm. It currently proves the override by `time.sleep(budget + 2)` in-tree,\n   so its cost is PINNED to the budget: at 300 s it would sleep 302 s. (At 20 s it already\n   costs 22.01 s — the single slowest unmarked-equivalent entry in the failing runs.) Move it\n   out-of-process onto the same generated-project helper the negative arm already uses, with a\n   small generated budget, so the arm costs seconds and the budget is free to be sized on\n   evidence instead of on this test's runtime.\n\n`timeout_func_only = true` is deliberately KEPT: it is not implicated in these crashes (the\ncost is all `call` time), and dropping it would newly bound local session fixtures — a\nbehaviour change beyond restoring what broke. Its effect on setup/teardown hang coverage is\nrecorded as a separate follow-up rather than folded in here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `pyproject.toml`'s `[tool.pytest.ini_options].timeout` is 300; checked by\n      `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py::test_the_configured_budget_is_the_measured_one`.\n- [ ] Both shared-tier lanes in `_build-and-test.yml` run at `--timeout=300`; checked by\n      `test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_the_shared_tier_lanes_carry_the_ini_timeout_budget`.\n- [ ] A test whose body outruns the ini budget is still killed by the ini alone; checked by\n      the existing negative arm `test_an_unmarked_over_budget_test_is_killed_by_the_ini_alone`.\n- [ ] `@pytest.mark.timeout(N, func_only=True)` still overrides the ini; checked by the\n      restructured marker-override arm, which must complete in under 30 s regardless of the\n      configured budget.\n- [ ] The `--timeout-method=thread` hang-guard sweep still passes; checked by\n      `test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_shared_pytest_suite_has_a_per_test_hang_guard`.\n- [ ] The ubuntu py3.13 default-suite leg completes with zero `worker '.*' crashed` /\n      `node down` lines; checked on the change's own Verified run.\n\n## Verification\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py -q\n    pytest tests/scripts -q -n 4 --dist worksteal","id":"3fa7-94ba-42aa-4623","parent_id":"","priority":0,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"The 20s per-test hang budget kills xdist workers on every CI run"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787418926070911001,"uuid":"6b8a24f7-07a5-48ef-9193-2656d21cf486"}